# --- discern harness ---
# Compiled agent files are generated by `discern refresh` from discern's
# built-in guidance + your [guidance].sources. They are build artifacts, not
# tracked: the reviewable source is your [guidance].sources (e.g. guidance.md),
# which IS tracked, so guidance changes show up in review as source diffs. A
# direct edit to a generated file is overwritten on the next refresh — and
# `discern status` / `discern finish` flag one that has drifted from its source,
# so it never silently goes stale (ADR 0034).
/AGENTS.md
/CLAUDE.md
/GEMINI.md
# Local rescue metadata/content written before discern overwrites a generated
# artifact that contains user edits. `discern status` points at these files; move
# durable guidance into guidance.md and durable skills into [skills].dir.
/.discern-rescue/
# Everything under .claude/ is generated, ephemeral, or machine-local — chiefly the
# materialized skills (.claude/skills/, copied/symlinked by `discern refresh`) and
# settings.local.json permission overrides — EXCEPT the shared settings.json, which
# is tracked. (Worktree checkouts default to a sibling dir OUTSIDE the repo, so they
# need no fencing here; a project that points
# [worktree].root back inside the repo at .claude/worktrees keeps them ignored by
# this rule.)
/.claude/*
!/.claude/settings.json
# Skills are also materialized into the cross-tool .agents/skills/ standard dir
# (Codex's repo path, Gemini's preferred alias) — generated, so ignore it too.
/.agents/skills/
# NOTE: `.mcp.json` (the project-scoped MCP servers `discern refresh` wires
# `discern mcp` into) is deliberately NOT listed here. It is shared, co-owned
# config that discern MERGES into (preserving your own servers) — like
# .claude/settings.json, not a wholesale-regenerated derivative like CLAUDE.md —
# so the team gets the server. Leave it tracked; never add it to this fragment.
